<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Turkish, the default.

    Every user-facing string in this app lives here so that values-ar/ and
    values-ku/ can exist at all. Before this file grew, most of the wording was
    hard-coded in MainActivity and — worse — composed inside TrackingRepository,
    a class with no Context and therefore no way to reach a resource, which made
    the persistent notification the one screen a driver stares at for eighteen
    hours and the one that could never be translated.

    Two conventions worth keeping:

      Distances and counts are passed in as already-formatted strings, not as
      numbers, so the formatter can pin Latin digits. %1$s not %1$d. An Arabic
      phone formatting "%d" yields ٨ beside a Latin plate number.

      Nothing here interpolates a plate, a reference or an order number into the
      middle of a sentence. Those are identifiers, they are never translated,
      and a sentence built around them reads badly in a language whose word
      order differs from Turkish.
-->
